      "writtenOn": "2019-05-02T13:30:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another thought is:\n\nint deb_check \u003d debouncing[c]\nwhile (deb_check) {\n  i \u003d __fls(deb_check)\n  deb_check \u0026\u003d ~BIT(i);\n  if (time_until(scan_time[scan_edge_index[c][i]], tnow) \u003e\u003d\n\t\t\t    (state[c] ? keyscan_config.debounce_down_us :\n\t\t\t\t\tkeyscan_config.debounce_up_us))\n    debouncing[c] \u0026\u003d ~BIT(i);\n}\n\n\nwhich will only check the set bits. Since the set columns are spare this will skip unnecessary loop iterations.\n\nThis is really more of a subjective call; I\u0027ll let you decide. I just wanted to give you the __fls option and time_until method choices :)",
